            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "block_label": "text",
          "block_content": "“Gears” (Wednesdays, 8 EST/PST, ★★☆☆), created by Mike Scully and Julie Thacker-Scully (“The Simpsons”), is neither original nor exciting; It’s an unchallenging and not very funny package of generational stereotypes and grating banter between Allen and Dennings. The two episodes made available for review feature dialogue so bland it could have been written by AI. They lack excitement in any way, but are not so achingly terrible they offend the senses. And considering both Allen’s track record and the recent spate of deeply disappointing multi-camera sitcoms on broadcast TV, that’s actually an achievement. Expectations are everything.",
